# Cosmetics inside Change Appearance (client/MANIFEST.md "Customise Character extras", BASE.md 62; owner 2026-10-20: "put all the options inside Change Appearance"). The separate Cosmetics panel of 0075 is gone: modules/game_outfit/outfit.lua now hands the overlay module game_outfitextras its radio group (addRow), a helper that clears the right-hand list (prepareList) and the "Only mine" sync, after the group is built; selecting a cosmetic row calls show(key), search and "Only mine" re-show it, a base row first calls leave(). data/styles/40-outfitwindow.otui makes room: window 796x720 (was 756x565, 729 with the old panel), preview 517x180, Configure and Change Appearance from y 214 and 456 px tall (Change Appearance 367 wide, value boxes at x 130 so longer row names fit), right-hand list 585 px tall. The Show Familiar box is hidden when the outfit packet has no familiars and the client has no familiar feature (10.98), Show Floor moves up into its place. Every call is guarded: without the module the rows are not there.
diff --git a/modules/game_outfit/outfit.lua b/modules/game_outfit/outfit.lua
